-## Not done yet (stage 2)
+## Changed in stage 2 (gate wired and tested)
 
-- Package names, binaries, identifiers and UI strings are still upstream's.
+Patch `0002-gate.patch` in the Netie repo, `ecosystem/overlays/control/`. Tests:
+`src/main/netie-control/*.test.ts` and `src/renderer/src/lib/netie-*.test.ts`, run with
+`npx vitest run --config config/vitest.config.ts src/main/netie-control src/renderer/src/lib/netie-*.test.ts`.
+
+- Board source. Every board surface (pop-out window, in-window drawer, sidebar counts) renders
+  the Netie Control board read from `NETIE_CONTROL_BOARD_URL`, in the shape
+  `netie.control.project_board` emits (ids only). `src/shared/netie-control-board.ts` carries the
+  same guards as the Python module: body keys refuse, remote-desktop kinds refuse, 12000 chars is
+  the budget, measured on the same ASCII-escaped text Python measures. Unconfigured, unreachable
+  or refused shows an empty board with a label saying why. The local agent-status store is no
+  longer board content, and the pop-out refreshes on its own clock.
+- Agent launch is off unless `NETIE_CONTROL_ALLOW_LOCAL_LAUNCH=1`. Agents start through the Crew
+  ticket runner, which this build does not reach yet, so the main process refuses every local
+  agent start with a label that names it (`src/shared/netie-crew-launch-gate.ts`): both PTY spawn
+  funnels, workspace create (the workspace is still made, its agent startup is stripped and the
+  result warns), terminal create and split, structured Claude and Codex sessions, source-control
+  text generation and model discovery, rate-limit and app-server probes, orchestration worker and
+  federated starts, dispatch with inject, automations, and app-typed launch text. An agent start
+  is recognised by the upstream launch fields or by an agent command line
+  (`src/shared/netie-agent-command-line.ts`, which sees through `sh -c`, `cmd /c`, PowerShell and
+  `npx`). Plain shells, setup scripts, non-agent commands and attach to a live session still work.
+  The renderer asks the same decision only to show the label without a round trip.
+- Model calls. Cloud dictation goes to `${NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL}/v1/audio/transcriptions`, default
+  `http://127.0.0.1:5000`, never to a provider host (`src/shared/netie-openvault-endpoint.ts`).
+  Every other model call the upstream makes runs through an agent CLI (commit message, PR fields,
+  branch names, model lists, usage probes) and is refused by the launch gate above.
+- Name. Window title, tray tooltip and notification titles read `APP_DISPLAY_NAME`
+  (`Netie Control`), `src/shared/app-display-name.ts`.
+- Upstream suites run under the documented development override through one setup file,
+  `config/scripts/vitest-netie-local-launch-override.ts`; the Netie tests clear it before each case
+  so the shipped default is what they prove.
+
+## Not done yet (stage 3)
+
+- Package name `orca`, binaries `orca` and `orca-dev`, `app.setName('Orca')`, data paths
+  (`~/.config/Orca`, `~/.orca`, `%APPDATA%\Orca`), electron-builder `productName`,
+  `appId` and executable names: each cascades into user data location or auto-update and
+  needs a migration before it moves.
+- UI string catalogs (`src/renderer/src/i18n/locales/*.json`, about 800 `Orca` strings in
+  `en.json`) and `TERM_PROGRAM=Orca`, which agent CLIs may detect.
+- Known limits of the launch gate: a person typing an agent command into a plain shell is not a
+  launch this app makes; agents whose names are also common tools (goose, kilo, hermes, pi, amp and
+  others) are recognised in a raw command only when bare or with an agent-shaped argument; account
+  login commands (`claude auth login`, `codex login`) are left alone; agent sessions a persistent
+  terminal daemon already hosted before the gate keep running.
+- Routing a launch to the Crew ticket runner: the runner is a Python API
+  (`netie.crew.run_open_ticket`) with no wire contract in the Netie repo yet.
+- Whether OpenVault needs a seat token for `/v1/audio/transcriptions`, and whether it
+  serves that route at all: not measured. The dictation key field stays as the cache the
+  TAS allows, never a second vault.
+- `api.anthropic.com` remains as a connectivity probe URL in `src/main/network/proxy-settings.ts`
+  and as the OAuth usage read (no model call). Claude, Codex, Copilot and Cursor account features
+  remain in the tree; agent use through them is refused while launch is off.
 - SECURITY, SUPPORT and CONTRIBUTING contacts and URLs still point at upstream.
 - Translated docs, changelogs and third-party notices are untouched.
-- Netie gate wiring: Board reads ids only through netie.control.project_board. Agent launches go through Crew ticket runner, never a second orchestrator.
